CYBERSECURITY AND INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY AGENCY
CYBERSECURITY ADVISORY AA26-258A

SUMMARY:
Vulnerability: CVE-2024-21887
Vendor: Ivanti
Product: Connect Secure / Policy Secure Gateway
Affected Versions: 9.x, 22.x
Vulnerability Type: Command Injection
Attack Vector: NETWORK
MITRE ATT&CK Technique: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)
Exploitation Status: CONFIRMED_EXPLOITATION_IN_WILD
Attack Outcome: EXPLOITED_SUCCESSFULLY
Affected Sector: Critical Infrastructure, Government, Technology
Publication Date: 2026-09-15

TECHNICAL OVERVIEW:
CISA and partner agencies have observed widespread scanning and successful exploitation targeting Ivanti Connect Secure instances. Attackers inject commands into web components to extract admin credentials, bypass multifactor authentication, and establish permanent web shells.

CISA DIRECTIVE:
Apply vendor patch immediately or disconnect public interfaces. Review network logs for outbound connections to suspect IP addresses.

Confidence: 0.96
